{{%/* Gash 3.0. Author: Maurizio Fonte <fonte.maurizio@gmail.com>

Stub overrides. A delegated function gets the one-line stub
`NAME() { __gash_call NAME "$@"; }` unless this file defines a template
named "stub/NAME": its text (the registry Function as data, leading and
trailing newlines trimmed) replaces the stub wherever the function is
defined (gash.sh, the module shims, the core shims). A shell-mutating
function (MATRIX class `shell-mutating`) uses one to keep its parent-shell
part (cd, history, eval of quoted exports) in Bash and call the binary
for the rest. Example:

{{% define "stub/NAME" %}}
NAME() {
    ...
    __gash_call {{% .Name %}} "$@"
}
{{% end %}}
